# 2. The path grammar

Every important location should be readable as:

```text
PROJECT → DOMAIN → WORKFLOW → PURPOSE → FILE
```

Examples:

```text
LRS → ASM → CHR21 → CONFIG → containers.yaml
LRS → ASM → CONTAINERS → FLYE2 → Dockerfile
LRS → ALIGN → results → figures
LRS → SV → configuration
```

This is the main memory strategy.

## Example

Instead of memorizing:

```text
/home/nicolas/lrs_benchmarking/final_report_files/snakemake_assemblers_benchmarking/benchmark_chr21_real/config/containers.yaml
```

remember:

```text
ASM → CHR21 → CONFIG → containers.yaml
```

Then the shell variable gives you:

```bash
"$ASMCONFIG/containers.yaml"
```

