# 4. One consistent shortcut language

All **directory navigation** shortcuts begin with:

```text
go-
```

All **project information / inspection** shortcuts begin with:

```text
lrs-
```

This makes them much easier to remember.

## Directory shortcuts

| Shortcut | Meaning | Destination |
|---|---|---|
| `go-lrs` | Go to repository root | `$LRS` |
| `go-asm` | Go to assembler project | `$ASM` |
| `go-chr21` | Go to current chr21 assembler workflow | `$CHR21` |
| `go-config` | Go to assembler config | `$ASMCONFIG` |
| `go-cont` | Go to assembler containers | `$ASMCONT` |
| `go-scripts` | Go to assembler scripts | `$ASMSCRIPTS` |
| `go-flye` | Go directly to Flye2 Docker context | `$ASMCONT/flye2` |
| `go-goldrush` | Go directly to GoldRush Docker context | `$ASMCONT/goldrush` |
| `go-ntlink` | Go directly to ntLink Docker context | `$ASMCONT/ntlink` |
| `go-verkko` | Go directly to Verkko2 Docker context | `$ASMCONT/verkko2` |
| `go-align` | Go to aligner benchmarking | `$ALIGN` |
| `go-sv` | Go to SV work | `$SV` |

## Information shortcuts

| Shortcut | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `lrs-map` | Open this project map in the terminal |
| `lrs-map-code` | Open this map in VS Code |
| `lrs-where` | Print the important project directories |
| `lrs-status` | Show Git status for the whole repository |
| `lrs-asm-status` | Show Git status only for assembler project |

### The mnemonic

```text
go-X      = take me to X
lrs-X     = show / inspect something about the project
