# 11. GitHub vs local-only policy

## 🟢 GitHub / source-controlled

These are generally reproducibility/source files:

```text
Snakefiles
*.smk
Dockerfiles
*.yaml / *.yml
reusable *.py
reusable *.sh
README / docs
small manifests / sample sheets
container definitions
workflow configuration
```

For the current assembler workflow, important GitHub candidates include:

```text
benchmark_chr21_real/Snakefile.assemblers
benchmark_chr21_real/config/config.assemblers.yaml
benchmark_chr21_real/config/containers.yaml

containers/flye2/Dockerfile
containers/goldrush/Dockerfile
containers/ntlink/Dockerfile
containers/verkko2/Dockerfile

scripts/check_assembler_container_definitions.sh
scripts/validate_containerized_chr21_workflow.sh

docs/PROJECT_MAP.md
docs/lrs_shortcuts.sh
```

---

## 🔴 Local / server only

Normally do **not** push:

```text
real FASTQ
BAM
assembly FASTA outputs
large intermediates
.snakemake/
.conda/
container build logs
Docker image archives
temporary outputs
large workflow results
```

For chr21:

```text
$CHR21/inputs/
$CHR21/results/
```

Think:

```text
CODE / CONFIG / DOCS  → GitHub
DATA / RESULTS        → local or server
```

